  "status": "published",
  "title": "SpaceX Gets Texas Air Permit as Cameron County Blocks Tax Break",
  "deck": "Texas authorized emissions from 43 gas-fired generators tied to the proposed $24 billion data center. Starbase will consider a separate tax break Dec. 9.",
  "category": "economy",
  "categoryLabel": "Economy",
  "type": "article",
  "author": "EP News",
  "publishedAt": "2026-11-21T13:14:00Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-11-21T13:14:00Z",
  "body": [
    "Texas environmental regulators issued an air permit Nov. 16 for 43 natural gas-fired generators tied to SpaceX’s proposed $24 billion data center and power plant in South Texas. The next day, Cameron County commissioners voted 3–2 against taking the company’s property tax break request to a public hearing.",
    "The Texas Commission on Environmental Quality’s permit letter authorizes emissions from the generators at the Boca Chica Facility if SpaceX builds and operates them as described in its registration. The agency’s technical review puts their combined generating capacity at about 1,456 megawatts and says SpaceX confirmed it would obtain a separate Title V operating permit.",
    "The county vote was on whether to post public notice that commissioners would consider the proposed abatement. SpaceX had sought a 10-year county property tax exemption and proposed fixed annual payments in lieu of taxes. The company estimated the project would create 500 jobs.",
    "SpaceX said after the vote that the annual payments would have made county revenue more predictable as the equipment lost taxable value. Commissioners’ decision ended consideration of the current county request before the proposed agreement reached a public hearing.",
    "The City of Starbase has scheduled its own hearing for Dec. 9 on a municipal tax abatement and a related economic development agreement. That hearing is the next scheduled public decision point for incentives tied to the project."
  ],
